KNOWNBUG msvc-stl
main.cpp
--cpp11 --unwind 8 --object-bits 12
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ padded to the field width: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Meaningful only with the MSVC STL (Windows), hence the tag msvc-stl, which
the other platforms exclude (elsewhere the #error makes it fail).
Symbolic execution did not end: setw (defined in the runtime) had no
model, num_put's sprintf_s (the UCRT's __stdio_common_vsprintf_s) had
none, Visual Studio's va_arg read the value as `(bv)(void *)7', which the
simplifier did not fold, and each locale-name copy (_Ntcts_dup_dbg,
_Maklocstr) could fail.  Checked with the MSVC 14.51 headers preprocessed
by cl and --winx64 on Linux: 10 s.  It needs more than the 256 objects of
the default --object-bits 8.
